    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76877" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλιμ-πετής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>falling back</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				3.30
			</span></i>; <i>recurrent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				57
			</span></i>: in early writers only in neut. as Adv., <i>back
				again</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἂψ ἐπὶ νῆας ἔεργε παλιμπετές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.395
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς . . ἐν νηῒ παλιμπετὲς ἀπονέωνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.27
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				294
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1250
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
